@@ -9,6 +9,21 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **Alembic `alter_column` emits CUBRID-compatible SQL for nullability, dropped
+  defaults and comments (#861)** — these changes went to Alembic's generic SQL, which
+  CUBRID rejects: `nullable=` emitted `ALTER COLUMN c SET/DROP NOT NULL`,
+  `server_default=None` emitted `DROP DEFAULT` (both syntax errors), and `comment=`
+  raised "can't render element of type ColumnComment", so any autogenerated
+  nullability change failed at `upgrade`. Nullability and comment changes now go
+  through `MODIFY` / `CHANGE` (a missing `existing_type` raises `ValueError`), and a
+  dropped default emits `ALTER COLUMN c SET DEFAULT NULL`, or two `MODIFY` statements
+  for a `NOT NULL` column. Because CUBRID 10.2/11.0 reset an attribute that `MODIFY`
+  omits and 11.2+ keep it, the definition now states `NULL` for a NOT NULL to
+  nullable change, `DEFAULT NULL` for a dropped default and `COMMENT ''` for a removed
+  comment; an existing column without a default no longer gets `DEFAULT NULL`. A
+  UNIQUE `create_index` in offline `--sql` mode raises the documented "live
+  connection" `CompileError` instead of `NoInspectionAvailable`.
+
 - **`literal_binds` and other compile options reach CAST operands, ON DUPLICATE KEY
   UPDATE values and collection members (#862)** — the nested `process()` calls in
   four places (`visit_cast`, both ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value paths and collection
